---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const lessons = (await getCollection('lessons')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const firstLesson = lessons[0];
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Agentic Engineering Workshop"
  description="Build SupportHub, a distributed customer support application, using Aspire, GitHub Copilot CLI, and HVE Core across seven feature steps."
>
  <article class="container workshop-intro">
    <h1>Agentic Engineering Workshop</h1>
    <p>
      Build <strong>SupportHub</strong>, a distributed customer support and ticket
      management application, using .NET Aspire, GitHub Copilot CLI, and
      Hypervelocity Engineering (HVE Core). The seven steps cover customer
      management, tickets, file attachments, activity and audit, SLA management,
      a support dashboard, and a final web and operations-console redesign.
    </p>
    <p>
      The application uses C# and ASP.NET Core APIs with a Blazor Interactive
      Server frontend. PostgreSQL stores customer and ticket data, Blob Storage
      holds attachments, Service Bus carries ticket events, Cosmos DB stores
      activity records, and Redis supports caching. Aspire orchestrates the
      services and local infrastructure and exposes health, logs, and traces.
    </p>
    <p>
      Run each step's four prompts separately with <code>/rpi-research</code>,
      <code>/rpi-plan</code>, <code>/rpi-implement</code>, and
      <code>/rpi-review</code> in Copilot CLI. Inspect the research and approve the
      plan before implementation. Use repository-local Aspire Skills to verify
      the running application, not just the build. Review may lead to another
      Research–Plan–Implement cycle and another review.
    </p>
    <p>
      Work in the SupportHub application repository, starting from its prepared
      Aspire baseline. Each feature branch builds on the previous one. After
      reviewing a feature, use the repository's <code>gh-stack</code> skill to
      prepare its stacked PR; submit only after explicit approval.
      The first lesson includes the baseline checks.
    </p>

    <section id="references" aria-labelledby="references-title">
      <h2 id="references-title">References</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://aspire.dev/">Aspire</a>
          — tools for running and observing the application and its services.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/hve-core">Hypervelocity Engineering (HVE Core)</a>
          — the skills and prompts used for the workshop workflow.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/github/copilot-cli">GitHub Copilot CLI</a>
          — the terminal-based coding agent used to run the prompts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/sinannar/agentic-engineering-experiment">SupportHub application repository</a>
          — the application, setup notes, and original workshop prompts.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="lessons" aria-label="Start the workshop">
      <a class="button" href={`${base}/lessons/${firstLesson.id}/`}>
        Start workshop
      </a>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .workshop-intro {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  section {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  li a {
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
</style>
